md`# brain-snapshot

A Cloud Brain recipe: once a day it fetches a list of public feeds and keeps what each one said as a public JSON file. It records. It makes no model call, ranks nothing and writes no summary: a notebook reads the files and does that.

| | |
|---|---|
| Worker | \`brain-x-snapshot\` |
| \`snapshot.run\` | procedure, the owner's own session. Fetches every source now and keeps today's files. Answers the day's index. |
| \`snapshot.sources\` | query, anyone. \`{ sources, default, keepDays }\`: the list in use, whether it is the list below, and how many days are kept. |
| \`snapshot.setSources\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ sources: [...] }\` replaces the list; \`{ sources: null }\` goes back to the list below. \`{ keepDays }\` sets how many days are kept (90 unless set). |
| Timer | each day at the first tick after 06:00 UTC, once (\`rows\`: \`ran/<day>\`). The tick is the wrapper's minute alarm, armed by the deployer's health check at deploy; the cron is declared as well. |
| Storage | files in \`brain-static\` under \`snapshot/<day>/\`, public, tag \`snapshot\`. \`rows\`: \`sources\`, \`keepDays\`, \`ran/<day>\`, \`day/<day>\`. |

To run it now: the **Run now** button below, in the owner's own session. From this checkout: \`BRAIN_BASE=cb4 bun tools/cloud-brain/brain.ts curl /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.run --owner -X POST\`. A token is refused.

## What is kept

Anyone reads these with no session. \`<day>\` is the UTC date, \`2026-10-09\`.

| Address | Holds |
|---|---|
| \`/static/snapshot/days.json\` | \`{ days: [{ day, ranAt, items, papers }] }\`, newest first; \`papers\` is the count in that day's \`papers.json\` |
| \`/static/snapshot/<day>/index.json\` | \`{ day, ranAt, sources: [{ name, tier, status, count, matched, of, bytes, ms, path, error, lookup }], papers: { count, path }, errors }\` |
| \`/static/snapshot/<day>/<source>.json\` | \`{ source, tier, url, day, fetchedAt, count, items }\` |
| \`/static/snapshot/<day>/papers.json\` | \`{ day, ranAt, count, papers: [{ id, url, title, summary, points, signals, via }] }\`: the papers with a signal seen that day (below) |

An item is \`{ id, title, source, tier }\` and, where the feed gives them, \`url points comments author published discussion summary papers\`. An Ask HN post has no \`url\`. \`published\` is an ISO time. \`summary\` is text, cut at 1500 characters. \`papers\` is the arXiv ids the item links to.

A feed's summary has its markup taken out, after its entities are read: a \`<\` that starts a tag name is read as a tag up to the next \`>\`, so \`p < 0.05 and n > 3\` is kept and \`a<b and c>d\` loses \`<b and c>\`. A title is text: \`The &lt;dialog&gt; element\` is kept as \`The <dialog> element\`, and so is markup a feed escaped into a title (\`new <i>results</i>\`). Only an Atom title that says \`type="html"\` or \`"xhtml"\` has markup taken out. An Atom entry's \`<source>\`, the feed it was copied from, is not read. Text from a JSON source is kept as it is.

- A second run on one day replaces that day's files: the last run is what is kept.
- A source that fails, or that has nothing to keep, writes no file. Its row in the index says why (\`status\`, \`error\`, \`count: 0\`), and a file an earlier run of that day made for it stays.
- Every source is fetched at the same time. Give one host one source: Reddit answered 429 to the second of two feeds, also 2 s apart (cb4, 2026-10-09), so its two subreddits are one feed.
- A failed source does not fail the run. The timer runs once a day and does not try again; \`snapshot.run\` does.
- \`of\` is how many items the feed held, \`matched\` how many passed \`keep\` and \`days\`, \`count\` how many were kept. \`matched\` above \`count\` means \`limit\` cut the list, unless the row has an \`error\`: a source whose file was refused has \`count: 0\` and its \`matched\`.
- \`errors\` in the index, and in the log line, names a write of \`index.json\`, \`papers.json\` or \`days.json\` that failed.
- The daily run drops the files of days older than \`keepDays\` with \`static.delete\` \`{ prefix: "snapshot/", before }\`. \`snapshot.run\` drops nothing.

## Papers

arXiv lists 600 to 900 new papers a day in these three categories (\`limit: 1000\`). Nobody reads that list, and its feed gives authors with no affiliation, so it cannot be cut down to known labs. \`arxiv.json\` is kept for looking a paper up (\`lookup: true\` in the index): do not read it whole. \`papers.json\` holds the papers that carry at least one signal, and says which:

| signal | means |
|---|---|
| \`votes:<source>\` | the paper is in a source that has \`papers: { min }\` with at least \`min\` points. Hugging Face's daily papers, 10, published in the last 3 days. |
| \`lab:<source>\` | an item of a \`research\` feed links to it (\`arxiv.org/abs\`, \`/pdf\`, \`/html\`, or \`huggingface.co/papers\`). |
| \`mention:<source>\` | an item of a \`blogger\` or \`aggregator\` source links to it. |

\`via\` is the items that linked to it. Title and summary come from the voting source, else from \`arxiv.json\` when the paper is in that day's list; a paper in neither, linked from an item only, has its id and \`via\` and nothing else. Papers are in order of how many signals they carry, then points.

\`papers.json\` is not the papers published that day. Hugging Face's list held 50 papers published on 11 dates, 2026-09-23 to 2026-10-07, when read on 2026-10-09; \`days: 3\` keeps the last three days of it, so a voted paper is in up to 3 days' files. A paper linked from an item is in each day's file that the item is in.

## Sources

A source is a row, not code: \`{ name, tier, url, kind }\`. The list is public, and each kept file names its source's address: do not give a source an address that carries a key.

- \`kind\`: \`rss\` or \`atom\` (one reader for both), or \`json\` with \`map\`, the path of each field in an item (\`"paper.id"\`), and \`items\`, the path of the list when it is not the whole answer. A \`map\` value with braces is a pattern: \`"https://huggingface.co/papers/{paper.id}"\`.
- \`tier\`: \`research\`, \`blogger\` or \`aggregator\`. Research and named writers lead. An aggregator says what people discuss.
- \`days\`: keep only items published in that many days before the run. A blog's feed holds its old posts; every \`research\` blog and every \`blogger\` here has \`days: 7\`, so most of them keep nothing on most days.
- \`keep\`: a pattern an item's text must match. arXiv's feed also lists replaced papers; \`keep\` leaves new and cross-listed ones.
- \`limit\`: at most this many items, 500 unless given.
- A list has 1 to 40 sources. One run is one invocation of the Worker: one fetch and one \`static.put\` for each source that keeps items, then three more writes, and one delete on the timer. The 21 here ran on cb4. 40 was not run, and the count was not measured against the plan's limit of subrequests in one invocation.
- \`papers: { min }\`: the items are papers, their \`id\` an arXiv id, and one with \`min\` points or more is in \`papers.json\`. \`lookup: true\`: the items are papers to look up, not to read.

Each source is fetched once a run, with the \`User-Agent\` \`${snapshotAgent}\`.

Measured from a Worker of cb4 on 2026-10-09 (\`tools/scratch/snapshot-probe\`): the arXiv API answered 429 "Rate exceeded" and its RSS feed 200, so the feed is used. Reddit's \`.json\` answered 403 and its \`.rss\` 200, so the feed is used, which gives no score; after about ten requests in an hour from the tests it answered 429 to each one. Anthropic and Meta AI have no feed at the addresses tried (404) and are not in the list. Gwern's feed has nothing after 2021 and is not in the list.`
// %%
viewof snapshotView = snapshotPanel({ base: client && client.base, client, owner: !!(session && session.owner) })
// %%
snapshotAgent = "lopecode-cloud-brain-snapshot/1 (+https://github.com/tomlarkworthy/lopecode)"
// %%
snapshotSources = {
  const blog = (name, url, tier = "blogger") => ({ name, tier, url, kind: "rss", days: 7 });
  return [
    { name: "arxiv", tier: "research", url: "https://rss.arxiv.org/rss/cs.AI+cs.LG+cs.CL", kind: "rss", keep: "Announce Type: (new|cross)", limit: 1000, lookup: true },
    { name: "hf-papers", tier: "research", url: "https://huggingface.co/api/daily_papers?limit=50", kind: "json", map: { id: "paper.id", title: "paper.title", url: "https://huggingface.co/papers/{paper.id}", points: "paper.upvotes", comments: "numComments", published: "publishedAt", summary: "paper.summary" }, days: 3, papers: { min: 10 } },
    blog("openai", "https://openai.com/news/rss.xml", "research"),
    blog("deepmind", "https://deepmind.google/blog/rss.xml", "research"),
    blog("google-research", "https://research.google/blog/rss/", "research"),
    blog("microsoft-research", "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/feed/", "research"),
    blog("bair", "https://bair.berkeley.edu/blog/feed.xml", "research"),
    blog("meta-engineering-ai", "https://engineering.fb.com/category/ai-research/feed/", "research"),
    blog("simon-willison", "https://simonwillison.net/atom/everything/"),
    blog("karpathy", "https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/feed/"),
    blog("karpathy-github", "https://karpathy.github.io/feed.xml"),
    blog("lilian-weng", "https://lilianweng.github.io/index.xml"),
    blog("sebastian-raschka", "https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/feed"),
    blog("import-ai", "https://jack-clark.net/feed/"),
    blog("eugene-yan", "https://eugeneyan.com/rss/"),
    blog("chip-huyen", "https://huyenchip.com/feed.xml"),
    blog("interconnects", "https://www.interconnects.ai/feed"),
    blog("hamel-husain", "https://hamel.dev/index.xml"),
    { name: "hn", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/search?tags=front_page&hitsPerPage=50", kind: "json", items: "hits", map: { id: "objectID", title: "title", url: "url", points: "points", comments: "num_comments", author: "author", published: "created_at", discussion: "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id={objectID}" } },
    { name: "reddit", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://www.reddit.com/r/MachineLearning+LocalLLaMA/top/.rss?t=day&limit=100", kind: "atom" },
    { name: "lobsters-ai", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://lobste.rs/t/ai.json", kind: "json", map: { id: "short_id", title: "title", url: "url", points: "score", comments: "comment_count", author: "submitter_user", published: "created_at", discussion: "comments_url", summary: "description_plain" } }
  ];
}
// %%
// Text of a feed field: entities read, markup taken out, entities of the markup's own text read.
// markup false: the field is text, so what its entities spell ("<dialog>") is kept.
snapshotText = (s, max = 1500, markup = true) => {
  const named = { lt: "<", gt: ">", quot: '"', apos: "'", amp: "&", nbsp: " ", mdash: "\u2014", ndash: "\u2013", hellip: "\u2026", lsquo: "\u2018", rsquo: "\u2019", ldquo: "\u201c", rdquo: "\u201d" };
  const point = (n, e) => (n >= 0 && n <= 0x10ffff ? String.fromCodePoint(n) : e);
  const entities = (t) => t.replace(/&(#x[0-9a-f]+|#\d+|[a-z]+);/gi, (e, k) => (k[0] !== "#" ? (named[k.toLowerCase()] ?? e) : point(/^#x/i.test(k) ? parseInt(k.slice(2), 16) : Number(k.slice(1)), e)));
  // A tag is < and a name; "p < 0.05 and n > 3" has none.
  const tags = (t) => t.replace(/<!--[\s\S]*?-->|<\/?[a-zA-Z][^<>]*>/g, " ");
  const once = entities(tags(String(s ?? "")));
  return snapshotPlain(entities(markup ? tags(once) : once), max);
}
// %%
// Text that is already text: spaces made single, cut.
snapshotPlain = (s, max = 1500) => String(s ?? "").replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim().slice(0, max)
// %%
// The arXiv papers a piece of text links to.
snapshotPapers = (text) => [...new Set([...String(text ?? "").replace(/&#x2F;|&#47;/gi, "/").matchAll(/(?:arxiv\.org\/(?:abs|pdf|html)\/|huggingface\.co\/papers\/)(\d{4}\.\d{4,5})/g)].map((m) => m[1]))]
// %%
// The items of an RSS or Atom feed. No XML parser runs in a Worker; a feed's items are flat, so each field is read by its tag.
snapshotFeed = (xml) => {
  const tag = (s, name) => (new RegExp("<" + name + "(?:\\s[^>]*)?>([\\s\\S]*?)</" + name + ">").exec(s) || [])[1] || "";
  // The link of an Atom entry: the one that is the page (rel alternate, or no rel), else the first.
  const href = (s) => {
    const links = [...s.matchAll(/<link\s[^>]*?>/g)].map((m) => ({ rel: (/\srel="([^"]*)"/.exec(m[0]) || [])[1], href: (/\shref="([^"]*)"/.exec(m[0]) || [])[1] })).filter((l) => l.href);
    return ((links.find((l) => !l.rel || l.rel === "alternate") || links[0] || {}).href) || "";
  };
  // A CDATA section is text: its < and & are written as entities, so a tag inside one is not read as a field.
  const flat = String(xml).replace(/<!\[CDATA\[([\s\S]*?)\]\]>/g, (_, t) => t.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;"));
  // An Atom entry's <source> is the feed it was copied from, with a title and id of its own.
  return flat.split(/<(?:item|entry)[\s>]/).slice(1).map((entry) => [entry, entry.replace(/<source[\s>][\s\S]*?<\/source>/g, "")]).map(([raw, s]) => ({
    id: snapshotText(tag(s, "guid") || tag(s, "id"), 500),
    // A title is text unless Atom says it is markup.
    title: snapshotText(tag(s, "title"), 500, /<title\s[^>]*\btype=["'](?:html|xhtml)["']/.test(s)),
    url: snapshotText(tag(s, "link") || href(s), 2000),
    author: snapshotText(tag(s, "dc:creator") || tag(tag(s, "author"), "name"), 200),
    published: snapshotText(tag(s, "pubDate") || tag(s, "published") || tag(s, "updated"), 100),
    summary: snapshotText(tag(s, "description") || tag(s, "summary") || tag(s, "content") || tag(s, "content:encoded")),
    raw
  }));
}
// %%
// The items of a JSON answer, each field read at the path the source's map names.
snapshotJson = (data, src) => {
  const at = (o, path) => String(path).split(".").reduce((v, k) => (v == null ? undefined : v[k]), o);
  const list = src.items ? at(data, src.items) : data;
  return (Array.isArray(list) ? list : []).map((o) => ({ ...Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(src.map || {}).map(([k, p]) => [k, /\{/.test(p) ? String(p).replace(/\{([^}]+)\}/g, (_, q) => at(o, q) ?? "") : at(o, p)])), raw: JSON.stringify(o) }));
}
// %%
// What one source's answer holds, in the kept shape: { of, matched, items }.
snapshotItems = (body, src, now = Date.now()) => {
  const raw = src.kind === "json" ? snapshotJson(JSON.parse(body), src) : snapshotFeed(body);
  const keep = src.keep ? new RegExp(src.keep) : null, since = src.days ? now - src.days * 86400000 : null;
  const items = [];
  let matched = 0;
  for (const r of raw) {
    if (keep && !keep.test(String(r.title) + " " + String(r.summary))) continue;
    const t = r.published ? Date.parse(r.published) : NaN;
    if (since !== null && !(t >= since)) continue;
    matched++;
    if (items.length >= (src.limit || 500)) continue;
    // A list of papers links to its own; any other item's links to papers are kept with it.
    const papers = src.papers || src.lookup ? [] : snapshotPapers(String(r.url) + " " + String(r.discussion) + " " + r.raw);
    const item = { id: String(r.id || r.url || r.title || ""), title: snapshotPlain(r.title, 500), url: r.url ? String(r.url) : undefined, points: r.points == null ? undefined : Number(r.points), comments: r.comments == null ? undefined : Number(r.comments), author: r.author ? String(r.author) : undefined, published: Number.isFinite(t) ? new Date(t).toISOString() : undefined, discussion: r.discussion ? String(r.discussion) : undefined, summary: snapshotPlain(r.summary) || undefined, papers: papers.length ? papers : undefined, source: src.name, tier: src.tier };
    if (item.id && item.title) items.push(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(item)));
  }
  return { of: raw.length, matched, items };
}
// %%
// The papers of a day that carry a signal: enough votes in a source of papers, or a link from another source's item.
snapshotSignals = (list, kept) => {
  const papers = new Map(), at = (id) => papers.get(id) || papers.set(id, { id, url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/" + id, signals: [], via: [] }).get(id);
  const add = (p, signal) => void (p.signals.includes(signal) || p.signals.push(signal));
  const known = new Map();
  for (const src of list)
    for (const item of kept.get(src.name) || []) {
      if (src.lookup) {
        const id = snapshotPapers(String(item.url))[0];
        if (id) known.set(id, item);
      } else if (src.papers) {
        if (!(item.points >= src.papers.min)) continue;
        add(Object.assign(at(item.id), { title: item.title, summary: item.summary, points: item.points }), "votes:" + src.name);
      } else
        for (const id of item.papers || []) {
          const p = at(id);
          add(p, (src.tier === "research" ? "lab:" : "mention:") + src.name);
          p.via.push({ source: src.name, title: item.title, url: item.discussion || item.url });
        }
    }
  for (const p of papers.values()) {
    const k = known.get(p.id);
    if (k && !p.title) Object.assign(p, { title: k.title, summary: k.summary });
  }
  return [...papers.values()].sort((a, b) => b.signals.length - a.signals.length || (b.points || 0) - (a.points || 0));
}
// %%
// A list of sources as the owner gave it, or the reason it is refused.
snapshotCheck = (list) => {
  if (!Array.isArray(list) || !list.length || list.length > 40) return "sources is a list of 1 to 40";
  const seen = new Set();
  for (const s of list) {
    if (!s || typeof s !== "object" || !/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$/.test(s.name || "") || seen.has(s.name)) return "each source has its own name of a-z, 0-9 and -";
    seen.add(s.name);
    if (!["research", "blogger", "aggregator"].includes(s.tier)) return s.name + ": tier is research, blogger or aggregator";
    if (!["json", "rss", "atom"].includes(s.kind)) return s.name + ": kind is json, rss or atom";
    try { if (new URL(s.url).protocol !== "https:") throw 0; } catch { return s.name + ": url is an https address"; }
    if (s.kind === "json" && (!s.map || typeof s.map !== "object" || !s.map.title)) return s.name + ": a json source has a map with a title";
    if (s.keep !== undefined) try { new RegExp(s.keep); } catch { return s.name + ": keep is a pattern"; }
    for (const k of ["days", "limit"]) if (s[k] !== undefined && !(typeof s[k] === "number" && s[k] > 0)) return `${s.name}: ${k} is a number above 0`;
    if (s.map !== undefined && (!s.map || typeof s.map !== "object" || !Object.values(s.map).every((v) => typeof v === "string"))) return s.name + ": each value of map is a path or a pattern";
    if (s.items !== undefined && typeof s.items !== "string") return s.name + ": items is a path";
    if (s.papers !== undefined && !(s.papers && typeof s.papers.min === "number")) return s.name + ": papers is { min }";
  }
  return null;
}
// %%
snapshotOps = {
  const STATIC = "com.lopecode.brain.static.";
  const dayOf = (now) => new Date(now).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  const put = async (path, value) => {
    const r = await xrpc.fetch(STATIC + "put", { method: "POST", params: { path, type: "application/json", public: "true", tags: "snapshot" }, body: new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(value)) });
    return r.ok ? null : `static.put ${path} ${r.status}`;
  };
  const sources = async () => (await rows.get("sources")) || snapshotSources;
  const keepDays = async () => (await rows.get("keepDays")) || 90;
  const one = async (src, day, now, kept) => {
    const t = Date.now(), row = { name: src.name, tier: src.tier, status: 0, count: 0, matched: 0, of: 0, bytes: 0, ms: 0, path: null, error: null, ...(src.lookup ? { lookup: true } : {}) };
    try {
      const r = await fetch(src.url, { headers: { "user-agent": snapshotAgent, accept: "application/json, application/atom+xml, application/rss+xml, application/xml;q=0.9, */*;q=0.5" } });
      const body = await r.text();
      Object.assign(row, { status: r.status, bytes: body.length });
      if (!r.ok) row.error = "the source answered " + r.status;
      else {
        const { of, matched, items } = snapshotItems(body, src, now);
        Object.assign(row, { of, matched, count: items.length });
        kept.set(src.name, items);
        if (items.length) {
          row.path = `snapshot/${day}/${src.name}.json`;
          row.error = await put(row.path, { source: src.name, tier: src.tier, url: src.url, day, fetchedAt: new Date(now).toISOString(), count: items.length, items });
          if (row.error) Object.assign(row, { path: null, count: 0 });
        }
      }
    } catch (e) {
      row.error = String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200);
    }
    row.ms = Date.now() - t;
    return row;
  };
  const run = async (now = Date.now()) => {
    const day = dayOf(now), list = await sources(), kept = new Map(), errors = [], tried = async (e) => void ((e = await e) && errors.push(e));
    const index = { day, ranAt: new Date(now).toISOString(), sources: await Promise.all(list.map((s) => one(s, day, now, kept))) };
    const items = index.sources.reduce((n, s) => n + s.count, 0), papers = snapshotSignals(list, kept);
    index.papers = { count: papers.length, path: `snapshot/${day}/papers.json` };
    await tried(put(index.papers.path, { day, ranAt: index.ranAt, count: papers.length, papers }));
    await rows.put("day/" + day, { day, ranAt: index.ranAt, items, papers: papers.length });
    await tried(put("snapshot/days.json", { days: (await rows.list("day/")).map((r) => r.value).sort((a, b) => (a.day < b.day ? 1 : -1)) }));
    index.errors = errors;
    // The index is written last, with what failed before it. Its own failure is in the answer and the log.
    await tried(put(`snapshot/${day}/index.json`, index));
    log({ at: "snapshot.run", day, items, papers: papers.length, sources: index.sources.map((s) => `${s.name}:${s.status}:${s.count}`).join(" "), ...(errors.length ? { error: errors.join("; ") } : {}) });
    return index;
  };
  // Days older than keepDays: their files, by prefix and date, and their rows.
  const prune = async (now) => {
    const before = new Date(now - (await keepDays()) * 86400000).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
    try {
      const { deleted } = await xrpc.procedure(STATIC + "delete", { prefix: "snapshot/", before });
      for (const k of ["day/", "ran/"]) for (const row of await rows.list(k)) if (row.key.slice(k.length) < before) await rows.delete(row.key);
      log({ at: "snapshot.prune", before, deleted });
    } catch (e) {
      log({ at: "snapshot.prune", before, error: String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200) });
    }
  };
  // The wrapper ticks once a minute. One run a day, at the first tick after 06:00 UTC.
  let ticked = null;
  const tick = async (now = Date.now()) => {
    const day = dayOf(now);
    if (new Date(now).getUTCHours() < 6 || ticked === day) return false;
    const first = await rows.putIfAbsent("ran/" + day, now);
    ticked = day;
    if (!first) return false;
    await prune(now);
    await run(now);
    return true;
  };
  return { run, tick, sources, keepDays };
}
// %%
snapshot_service = cloudflare.Service(
  "snapshot",
  async (request) => {
    const json = (status, body) => new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    const what = new URL(request.url).pathname.split(".").pop();
    if (what === "run") return json(200, await snapshotOps.run());
    if (what === "sources") return json(200, { sources: await snapshotOps.sources(), default: !(await rows.get("sources")), keepDays: await snapshotOps.keepDays() });
    if (what === "setSources") {
      const body = await request.json().catch(() => null);
      if (!body || typeof body !== "object") return json(400, { error: "InvalidRequest", message: "{ sources }" });
      if (body.keepDays !== undefined) {
        if (!(Number.isInteger(body.keepDays) && body.keepDays >= 1 && body.keepDays <= 3650)) return json(400, { error: "InvalidRequest", message: "keepDays is a whole number of days, 1 to 3650" });
        await rows.put("keepDays", body.keepDays);
        if (body.sources === undefined) return json(200, { keepDays: body.keepDays });
      }
      if (body.sources === null) return (await rows.delete("sources")), json(200, { sources: snapshotSources.length, default: true });
      const bad = snapshotCheck(body.sources);
      if (bad) return json(400, { error: "InvalidRequest", message: bad });
      await rows.put("sources", body.sources);
      return json(200, { sources: body.sources.length, default: false });
    }
    return json(404, { error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: "snapshot.run, snapshot.sources and snapshot.setSources" });
  },
  {
    crons: ["0 6 * * *"],
    // A cron event carries its time; the wrapper's minute alarm does not.
    scheduled: (event) => snapshotOps.tick((event && event.scheduledTime) || Date.now()),
    calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.static.put", "com.lopecode.brain.static.delete"],
    methods: {
      "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.run": { type: "procedure", allow: "caller.session" },
      "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.sources": { type: "query", who: "anyone" },
      "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.setSources": { type: "procedure", allow: "caller.session" }
    }
  }
)
// %%
snapshot_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", snapshot_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced snapshot_service";
}
// %%
// The days a Brain has kept, and what one day holds. Reads the public files; no session is needed. The owner runs it now.
snapshotPanel = ({ base, client, owner = false, fetch: send = (...a) => fetch(...a) } = {}) => {
  const muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
  if (!base) return Object.assign(htl.html`<i style=${muted}>Open this on a Brain to see its snapshots.</i>`, { value: null });
  const root = String(base).replace(/\/$/, "") + "/static/snapshot/", box = htl.html`<div></div>`, note = htl.html`<div style=${muted}></div>`;
  const el = Object.assign(htl.html`<div>${box}${note}</div>`, { value: null });
  const get = async (path) => { const r = await send(root + path); return r.ok ? r.json() : null; };
  const link = (u) => (u ? htl.html`<a href=${u} target="_blank">json</a>` : "");
  const load = async () => {
    const days = ((await get("days.json")) || { days: [] }).days;
    // One run at a time: the button is off until the run settles (a new one is drawn when it does).
    const now = owner && client ? Inputs.button("Run now", { reduce: () => {
      const b = now.querySelector("button");
      if (b.disabled) return;
      b.disabled = true;
      void client.procedure("snapshot.run", {}).then(() => el.load(), (e) => void ((b.disabled = false), (note.textContent = String((e && e.message) || e))));
    } }) : "";
    // The panel's one input event is its own, in draw.
    if (now) now.addEventListener("input", (e) => e.stopPropagation());
    if (!days.length) return void box.replaceChildren(htl.html`<i style=${muted}>No snapshot yet.</i>`, now);
    const pick = Inputs.select(days, { label: "Day", format: (d) => `${d.day}  (${d.items} items)` });
    const table = htl.html`<div></div>`;
    const draw = async () => {
      const index = await get(pick.value.day + "/index.json");
      table.replaceChildren(Inputs.table((index ? index.sources : []).map((s) => ({ source: s.name, tier: s.tier, kept: s.count, of: s.of, status: s.status, note: [s.error, !s.error && s.matched > s.count ? `cut from ${s.matched}` : "", s.lookup ? "to look up" : ""].filter(Boolean).join("; "), file: s.path ? root.replace(/snapshot\/$/, "") + s.path : "" })), { format: { file: link }, layout: "auto" }));
      note.replaceChildren(...(index ? [`ran ${index.ranAt}`, ...(index.papers ? [`, ${index.papers.count} papers with a signal `, link(root.replace(/snapshot\/$/, "") + index.papers.path)] : []), ...(index.errors && index.errors.length ? [`. Not written: ${index.errors.join("; ")}`] : [])] : []));
      // The value is the day's index. The select's own event is stopped below, so this is the one a cell hears.
      el.value = index;
      el.dispatchEvent(new Event("input", { bubbles: true }));
    };
    pick.addEventListener("input", (e) => (e.stopPropagation(), draw().catch(failed)));
    box.replaceChildren(pick, now, table);
    await draw();
  };
  const failed = (e) => void (note.textContent = "The snapshot files could not be read: " + String((e && e.message) || e));
  el.load = () => load().catch(failed);
  el.ready = el.load();
  return el;
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
snapshotRig = async ({ feeds = {}, rows = new Map(), fail = null } = {}) => {
  const files = new Map(), asked = [], dropped = [];
  const sim = await simulate(snapshot_service, {
    rows,
    secrets: { BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    fetch: async (request) => {
      asked.push({ url: request.url, agent: request.headers.get("user-agent") });
      const f = feeds[request.url];
      if (f === undefined) throw new Error("no route to host");
      return typeof f === "number" ? new Response("refused", { status: f }) : new Response(typeof f === "string" ? f : JSON.stringify(f));
    },
    core: async (request) => {
      const u = new URL(request.url);
      if (u.pathname.endsWith("static.delete")) return dropped.push(await request.json()), Response.json({ deleted: 2, paths: [] });
      if (fail && fail(u.searchParams.get("path"))) return Response.json({ error: "Forbidden" }, { status: 403 });
      files.set(u.searchParams.get("path"), { public: u.searchParams.get("public"), tags: u.searchParams.get("tags"), caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), value: JSON.parse(await request.text()) });
      return Response.json({ path: u.searchParams.get("path") });
    }
  });
  const call = async (name, body, caller = "owner") => {
    const r = await sim.fetch("https://snapshot.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.snapshot." + name, { method: body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": caller }, body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  return { sim, files, asked, dropped, rows, call };
}
// %%
snapshotFixtures = ({
  rss: `<?xml version="1.0"?><rss><channel><title>Feed</title><link>https://blog.example/</link>
<item><title>A &amp; B: <![CDATA[new <i>results</i>]]></title><link>https://blog.example/a</link><guid isPermaLink="false">a-1</guid><dc:creator>Ada</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#39;s &lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
<item><title>Old post</title><link>https://blog.example/old</link><guid>old-1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Jan 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>old</description></item>
</channel></rss>`,
  atom: `<?xml version="1.0"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>r/x</title>
<entry><author><name>/u/ada</name></author><content type="html">&lt;div&gt;Body &amp;amp; more&lt;/div&gt;</content><id>t3_1</id><link href="https://www.reddit.com/r/x/comments/1/?a=1&amp;b=2" /><updated>2026-10-09T01:00:00+00:00</updated><published>2026-10-09T01:00:00+00:00</published><title>[D] A thread</title></entry></feed>`
})
// %%
test_a_feed_item_is_read_by_its_tags_with_markup_and_entities_taken_out = {
  const now = Date.parse("2026-10-09T06:00:00Z");
  const rss = snapshotItems(snapshotFixtures.rss, { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", kind: "rss", days: 7 }, now);
  expect(rss).toEqual({ of: 2, matched: 1, items: [{ id: "a-1", title: "A & B: new <i>results</i>", url: "https://blog.example/a", author: "Ada", published: "2026-10-08T16:00:00.000Z", summary: "It's bold .", source: "blog", tier: "blogger" }] });
  // Without `days` the old post is kept as well.
  expect(snapshotItems(snapshotFixtures.rss, { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", kind: "rss" }, now).items.map((i) => i.id)).toEqual(["a-1", "old-1"]);
  const atom = snapshotItems(snapshotFixtures.atom, { name: "reddit-x", tier: "aggregator", kind: "atom" }, now);
  expect(atom.items).toEqual([{ id: "t3_1", title: "[D] A thread", url: "https://www.reddit.com/r/x/comments/1/?a=1&b=2", author: "/u/ada", published: "2026-10-09T01:00:00.000Z", summary: "Body & more", source: "reddit-x", tier: "aggregator" }]);
  // keep, limit, and a summary cut at 1500 characters.
  const many = `<rss>${[1, 2, 3, 4].map((n) => `<item><title>T${n}</title><guid>${n}</guid><description>Announce Type: ${n % 2 ? "new" : "replace"} ${"x".repeat(3000)}</description></item>`).join("")}</rss>`;
  const kept = snapshotItems(many, { name: "arxiv", tier: "research", kind: "rss", keep: "Announce Type: (new|cross)", limit: 1 }, now);
  expect([kept.of, kept.matched, kept.items.map((i) => i.id), kept.items[0].summary.length]).toEqual([4, 2, ["1"], 1500]);
  // An Atom entry's link is the page: rel alternate or no rel, wherever it comes. A title that says it is html has its markup taken out.
  // The feed an entry was copied from has a title and an id of its own, which are not the entry's.
  expect(snapshotFeed('<feed><entry><source><id>other</id><title>Other feed</title><link href="https://o.example/"/></source><id>1</id><title>Mine</title><link href="https://a.example/mine"/></entry></feed>')[0]).toMatchObject({ id: "1", title: "Mine", url: "https://a.example/mine" });
  const entry = (links) => snapshotFeed(`<feed><entry><id>1</id><title type="html"><![CDATA[Fast <em>&amp;</em> small </title><x>]]></title>${links}</entry></feed>`)[0];
  expect(entry('<link rel="self" href="https://a.example/feed"/><link rel="alternate" href="https://a.example/post"/>')).toMatchObject({ title: "Fast & small", url: "https://a.example/post" });
  expect(entry('<link rel="replies" href="https://a.example/c"/><link href="https://a.example/post"/>').url).toBe("https://a.example/post");
  expect(entry('<link rel="enclosure" href="https://a.example/a.mp3"/>').url).toBe("https://a.example/a.mp3");
  return "rss, atom, keep, days, limit";
}
// %%
test_text_keeps_a_comparison_and_reads_hex_and_named_entities = {
  expect(snapshotText("p &lt; 0.05 and n &gt; 3")).toBe("p < 0.05 and n > 3");
  expect(snapshotText("p < 0.05 <b>bold</b> <!-- no --> x")).toBe("p < 0.05 bold x");
  expect(snapshotText("It&#x2019;s &#8212; caf&#xE9; &mdash; &hellip;&nbsp;&unknown; &#x110000;")).toBe("It\u2019s \u2014 caf\u00e9 \u2014 \u2026 &unknown; &#x110000;");
  // Escaped twice: markup written about, not markup.
  expect(snapshotText("&amp;lt;div&amp;gt; in a title")).toBe("<div> in a title");
  // Escaped once: markup in a summary, text in a title.
  expect(snapshotText("Vec&lt;T&gt; and <b>more</b>")).toBe("Vec and more");
  expect(snapshotText("Vec&lt;T&gt; and Option&lt;Box&lt;T&gt;&gt; in Rust", 500, false)).toBe("Vec<T> and Option<Box<T>> in Rust");
  const feed = snapshotItems("<rss><item><guid>1</guid><title>The &lt;dialog&gt; element, AT&amp;amp;T</title><description>&lt;p&gt;About &lt;b&gt;it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></rss>", { name: "f", tier: "blogger", kind: "rss" }).items[0];
  expect([feed.title, feed.summary]).toEqual(["The <dialog> element, AT&T", "About it"]);
  // A JSON source's text is text: nothing in it is a tag or an entity.
  const item = snapshotItems(JSON.stringify([{ id: "1", title: "Why a<b and c>d &amp; more", summary: "x <i>y</i>" }]), { name: "j", tier: "aggregator", kind: "json", map: { id: "id", title: "title", summary: "summary" } }).items[0];
  expect([item.title, item.summary]).toEqual(["Why a<b and c>d &amp; more", "x <i>y</i>"]);
  return "8 texts";
}
// %%
test_a_json_source_is_read_by_the_paths_its_map_names = {
  const hn = snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "hn"), hf = snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "hf-papers");
  const a = snapshotItems(JSON.stringify({ hits: [{ objectID: "7", title: "Show HN", url: null, points: 12, num_comments: 3, author: "pg", created_at: "2026-10-09T00:00:00Z" }, { objectID: "8" }] }), hn);
  expect(a).toEqual({ of: 2, matched: 2, items: [{ id: "7", title: "Show HN", points: 12, comments: 3, author: "pg", published: "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z", discussion: "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=7", source: "hn", tier: "aggregator" }] });
  const b = snapshotItems(JSON.stringify([{ paper: { id: "2610.1", title: "A paper", upvotes: 5, summary: "An\nabstract" }, numComments: 0, publishedAt: "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z" }, { paper: { id: "2609.9", title: "An old paper", upvotes: 90, summary: "old" }, numComments: 0, publishedAt: "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z" }]), hf, Date.parse("2026-10-09T06:00:00Z"));
  // The list holds weeks of papers; one published more than 3 days before the run is not kept, whatever its votes.
  expect([b.of, b.matched]).toEqual([2, 1]);
  expect(b.items).toEqual([{ id: "2610.1", title: "A paper", url: "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.1", points: 5, comments: 0, published: "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z", summary: "An abstract", source: "hf-papers", tier: "research" }]);
  // An answer that is not the list the source names gives nothing.
  expect(snapshotItems("{}", hn)).toEqual({ of: 0, matched: 0, items: [] });
  return "hn, hf-papers";
}
// %%
test_a_run_keeps_one_public_file_a_source_and_a_failed_source_does_not_stop_it = {
  const sources = [
    { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss", days: 7 },
    { name: "quiet", tier: "blogger", url: "https://quiet.example/feed", kind: "rss", days: 7 },
    { name: "refused", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://refused.example/top.json", kind: "json", map: { id: "id", title: "title" } },
    { name: "down", tier: "research", url: "https://down.example/feed", kind: "rss" },
    { name: "broken", tier: "research", url: "https://broken.example/x.json", kind: "json", map: { id: "id", title: "title" } }
  ];
  const rig = await snapshotRig({ rows: new Map([["sources", sources]]), feeds: { "https://blog.example/feed": snapshotFixtures.rss.replace(/Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT/, new Date().toUTCString()), "https://quiet.example/feed": "<rss></rss>", "https://refused.example/top.json": 403, "https://broken.example/x.json": "<html>" } });
  let out;
  const lines = await logged(async () => void (out = await rig.call("run", {})));
  // The day the Worker read from its clock.
  const day = out.data.day;
  expect(out.status).toBe(200);
  expect(out.data.sources.map((s) => [s.name, s.status, s.count, s.path, s.error && s.error.slice(0, 22)])).toEqual([
    ["blog", 200, 1, `snapshot/${day}/blog.json`, null], ["quiet", 200, 0, null, null], ["refused", 403, 0, null, "the source answered 40"], ["down", 0, 0, null, "no route to host"], ["broken", 200, 0, null, expect.any(String)]
  ]);
  // One fetch a source. (A browser drops User-Agent from a Request, so the header is not seen under simulate.)
  expect(rig.asked.map((a) => a.url)).toEqual(sources.map((s) => s.url));
  // Only the source with items wrote a file; the index and the list of days are written whatever happened.
  expect([...rig.files.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`snapshot/${day}/blog.json`, `snapshot/${day}/index.json`, `snapshot/${day}/papers.json`, "snapshot/days.json"].sort());
  expect([out.data.papers, out.data.errors, rig.dropped]).toEqual([{ count: 0, path: `snapshot/${day}/papers.json` }, [], []]);
  const file = rig.files.get(`snapshot/${day}/blog.json`);
  expect([file.public, file.tags]).toEqual(["true", "snapshot"]);
  expect(file.value).toMatchObject({ source: "blog", tier: "blogger", day, count: 1, items: [{ id: "a-1", source: "blog" }] });
  expect(rig.files.get("snapshot/days.json").value).toEqual({ days: [{ day, ranAt: out.data.ranAt, items: 1, papers: 0 }] });
  // One line a run: names, statuses and counts, nothing a source said.
  expect(lines).toContainEqual({ at: "snapshot.run", day, items: 1, papers: 0, sources: "blog:200:1 quiet:200:0 refused:403:0 down:0:0 broken:200:0", worker: "brain-x-snapshot", ray: "" });
  // A second run the same day writes the same paths again.
  rig.files.clear();
  await rig.call("run", {});
  expect(rig.files.has(`snapshot/${day}/blog.json`)).toBe(true);
  expect(rig.files.get("snapshot/days.json").value.days.length).toBe(1);
  // A write the file store refuses is in the answer and the log line; a source's own is on its row.
  const poor = await snapshotRig({ rows: new Map([["sources", [{ ...sources[0], days: undefined }]]]), feeds: { "https://blog.example/feed": snapshotFixtures.rss }, fail: (path) => !path.endsWith("papers.json") });
  let bad;
  const said = await logged(async () => void (bad = (await poor.call("run", {})).data));
  expect(bad.sources[0]).toMatchObject({ count: 0, path: null, error: `static.put snapshot/${bad.day}/blog.json 403` });
  expect(bad.errors).toEqual(["static.put snapshot/days.json 403", `static.put snapshot/${bad.day}/index.json 403`]);
  expect(said.filter((l) => l.at === "snapshot.run").map((l) => l.error)).toContain(bad.errors.join("; "));
  return "5 sources, 1 file";
}
// %%
test_papers_are_the_ones_with_votes_a_lab_link_or_a_mention = {
  const day = new Date().toISOString(), paper = (id, upvotes) => ({ paper: { id, title: "HF " + id, upvotes, summary: "s" + id }, numComments: 0, publishedAt: day });
  const arxiv = (id) => `<item><title>arXiv ${id}</title><link>https://arxiv.org/abs/${id}</link><guid>oai:arXiv.org:${id}v1</guid><description>Announce Type: new Abstract ${id}</description></item>`;
  const sources = [
    { ...snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "arxiv"), url: "https://arxiv.example/rss" },
    { ...snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "hf-papers"), url: "https://hf.example/papers" },
    { name: "lab", tier: "research", url: "https://lab.example/feed", kind: "rss" },
    { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "atom" },
    { ...snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "hn"), url: "https://hn.example/top" }
  ];
  const rig = await snapshotRig({ rows: new Map([["sources", sources]]), feeds: {
    "https://arxiv.example/rss": `<rss>${["2610.00001", "2610.00002", "2610.00003", "2610.00009"].map(arxiv).join("")}</rss>`,
    "https://hf.example/papers": [paper("2610.00001", 40), paper("2610.00004", 10), paper("2610.00005", 9)],
    // A link in the item's own markup, escaped as a feed escapes it.
    "https://lab.example/feed": `<rss><item><title>Our new model</title><link>https://lab.example/model</link><guid>m</guid><description>&lt;a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.00002v2"&gt;paper&lt;/a&gt;</description></item></rss>`,
    "https://blog.example/feed": `<feed><entry><id>b1</id><title>Notes</title><link href="https://blog.example/notes"/><content type="html">&lt;a href="https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.00001"&gt;this&lt;/a&gt; and https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.12345</content></entry></feed>`,
    "https://hn.example/top": { hits: [{ objectID: "9", title: "A paper on HN", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.00002", points: 300 }, { objectID: "10", title: "Ask HN", story_text: "see arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;2610.00003" }] }
  } });
  const out = (await rig.call("run", {})).data, got = rig.files.get(out.papers.path).value;
  expect(out.papers.count).toBe(5);
  expect(got.papers.map((p) => [p.id, p.signals, p.title, p.points])).toEqual([
    ["2610.00001", ["votes:hf-papers", "mention:blog"], "HF 2610.00001", 40],
    ["2610.00002", ["lab:lab", "mention:hn"], "arXiv 2610.00002", undefined],
    ["2610.00004", ["votes:hf-papers"], "HF 2610.00004", 10],
    // Not in the day's list: an id and who linked it.
    ["2509.12345", ["mention:blog"], undefined, undefined],
    ["2610.00003", ["mention:hn"], "arXiv 2610.00003", undefined]
  ]);
  expect(got.papers[1]).toMatchObject({ url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.00002", summary: "Announce Type: new Abstract 2610.00002", via: [{ source: "lab", title: "Our new model", url: "https://lab.example/model" }, { source: "hn", title: "A paper on HN", url: "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=9" }] });
  // Under the threshold, or linked by nobody: not there. The whole list is kept and marked.
  expect(got.papers.some((p) => ["2610.00005", "2610.00009"].includes(p.id))).toBe(false);
  expect(out.sources.map((s) => [s.name, s.count, !!s.lookup])).toEqual([["arxiv", 4, true], ["hf-papers", 3, false], ["lab", 1, false], ["blog", 1, false], ["hn", 2, false]]);
  expect(rig.files.get(out.sources[4].path).value.items.map((i) => i.papers)).toEqual([["2610.00002"], ["2610.00003"]]);
  return "5 papers, 3 signals";
}
// %%
test_the_timer_runs_once_a_day_after_six = {
  const rig = await snapshotRig({ rows: new Map([["sources", [{ name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss" }]]]), feeds: { "https://blog.example/feed": snapshotFixtures.rss } });
  // A cron event carries its time, and the tick reads that.
  const at = async (iso, sim = rig.sim) => (await sim.scheduled({ scheduledTime: Date.parse(iso) }), rig.asked.length);
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T05:59:00Z")).toBe(0);
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T06:00:30Z")).toBe(1);
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T06:01:30Z")).toBe(1);
  expect([...rig.files.keys()]).toContain("snapshot/2026-10-09/blog.json");
  // Another instance of the Worker the same day finds the row and does not run.
  const second = await snapshotRig({ rows: rig.rows, feeds: {} });
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T09:00:00Z", second.sim)).toBe(1);
  expect(second.asked.length).toBe(0);
  expect(await at("2026-10-10T07:00:00Z")).toBe(2);
  // Each timed run drops what is older than keepDays, files by prefix and date, and the rows of those days.
  expect(rig.dropped).toEqual([{ prefix: "snapshot/", before: "2026-07-11" }, { prefix: "snapshot/", before: "2026-07-12" }]);
  expect((await rig.call("setSources", { keepDays: 1 })).data).toEqual({ keepDays: 1 });
  expect((await rig.call("setSources", { keepDays: 0 })).status).toBe(400);
  expect(await at("2026-10-12T07:00:00Z")).toBe(3);
  expect([rig.dropped[2], [...rig.rows.keys()].filter((k) => /^(day|ran)\//.test(k)).sort()]).toEqual([{ prefix: "snapshot/", before: "2026-10-11" }, ["day/2026-10-12", "ran/2026-10-12"]]);
  // A tick whose row write failed is tried again at the next one.
  const flaky = await snapshotRig({ rows: Object.assign(new Map([["sources", [{ name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss" }]]]), { has: () => { throw new Error("rows are away"); } }), feeds: { "https://blog.example/feed": snapshotFixtures.rss } });
  await flaky.sim.scheduled({ scheduledTime: Date.parse("2026-10-09T06:00:30Z") }).catch(() => null);
  delete flaky.rows.has;
  await flaky.sim.scheduled({ scheduledTime: Date.parse("2026-10-09T06:01:30Z") });
  expect(flaky.asked.length).toBe(1);
  return "3 runs in 4 days";
}
// %%
test_the_owner_sets_the_sources_and_a_bad_list_is_refused = {
  const rig = await snapshotRig();
  expect((await rig.call("sources")).data).toEqual({ sources: snapshotSources, default: true, keepDays: 90 });
  const mine = [{ name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss", days: 7 }];
  expect(await rig.call("setSources", { sources: mine })).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { sources: 1, default: false } });
  expect((await rig.call("sources")).data).toEqual({ sources: mine, default: false, keepDays: 90 });
  for (const bad of [[], [{ ...mine[0], name: "Blog" }], [mine[0], mine[0]], [{ ...mine[0], tier: "news" }], [{ ...mine[0], kind: "html" }], [{ ...mine[0], url: "http://blog.example/" }], [{ ...mine[0], kind: "json" }], [{ ...mine[0], keep: "(" }], [{ ...mine[0], days: "7" }], [{ ...mine[0], days: 0 }], [{ ...mine[0], limit: -1 }], [{ ...mine[0], limit: NaN }], [{ ...mine[0], kind: "json", map: { id: 1 } }], [{ ...mine[0], kind: "json", map: { id: "id" }, items: 3 }], [{ ...mine[0], papers: {} }], "x"])
    expect((await rig.call("setSources", { sources: bad })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.call("setSources", { sources: null })).data).toEqual({ sources: snapshotSources.length, default: true });
  expect((await rig.call("nope", {})).status).toBe(404);
  // The list this module ships is one the check accepts.
  expect(snapshotCheck(snapshotSources)).toBe(null);
  expect(new Set(snapshotSources.map((s) => s.tier))).toEqual(new Set(["research", "blogger", "aggregator"]));
  return snapshotSources.length + " default sources";
}
// %%
test_snapshot_declares_its_rules_its_timer_and_two_calls = {
  const { meta } = await snapshot_service.emit();
  expect(meta.worker).toBe("brain-x-snapshot");
  expect([meta.calls, meta.secrets, meta.crons]).toEqual([["com.lopecode.brain.static.delete", "com.lopecode.brain.static.put"], [], ["0 6 * * *"]]);
  const N = "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.";
  const ask = (m, caller, via = "") => decide(meta.access[N + m], { caller: callerOf({ caller, via }), origin: callerOf({ caller, via }), request: { params: {} } }).allow;
  expect([ask("run", "owner", "session"), ask("run", "owner", "token"), ask("run", "token:laptop"), ask("run", "worker:brain-x-echo"), ask("run", "anonymous")]).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect([ask("setSources", "owner", "session"), ask("setSources", "did:plc:friend"), ask("setSources", "anonymous")]).toEqual([true, false, false]);
  expect([ask("sources", "anonymous"), ask("sources", "did:plc:friend")]).toEqual([true, true]);
  return meta.worker;
}
// %%
test_the_panel_lists_the_days_and_the_sources_of_one = {
  const files = {
    "https://b.example/static/snapshot/days.json": { days: [{ day: "2026-10-09", ranAt: "2026-10-09T06:00:10.000Z", items: 3 }] },
    "https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/index.json": { day: "2026-10-09", ranAt: "2026-10-09T06:00:10.000Z", sources: [{ name: "hn", tier: "aggregator", status: 200, count: 3, of: 30, path: "snapshot/2026-10-09/hn.json", error: null }, { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", status: 403, count: 0, of: 0, path: null, error: "the source answered 403" }] }
  };
  files["https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/index.json"].sources[0].matched = 40;
  Object.assign(files["https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/index.json"], { papers: { count: 4, path: "snapshot/2026-10-09/papers.json" }, errors: ["static.put snapshot/days.json 403"] });
  const ran = [], send = async (u) => (files[u] ? Response.json(files[u]) : new Response("", { status: 404 }));
  const el = snapshotPanel({ base: "https://b.example/", fetch: send, owner: true, client: { procedure: async (name) => void ran.push(name) } });
  let heard = 0;
  el.addEventListener("input", () => heard++);
  await el.ready;
  // One input event a draw, after the value is set.
  expect([el.value.sources.length, heard]).toEqual([2, 1]);
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("ran 2026-10-09T06:00:10.000Z, 4 papers with a signal");
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("cut from 40");
  // A row with an error is not said to be cut.
  files["https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/index.json"].sources[1].matched = 2;
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("Not written: static.put snapshot/days.json 403");
  expect([...el.querySelectorAll("a")].map((a) => a.href)).toEqual(["https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/hn.json", "https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/papers.json"]);
  // Run now calls the Brain and reads the days again. A reader who is not the owner has no button.
  const button = el.querySelector("button");
  button.click();
  // Off until the run settles: a second press does nothing.
  expect(button.disabled).toBe(true);
  button.click();
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 50));
  expect(el.textContent).not.toContain("cut from 2");
  expect(el.querySelector("button").disabled).toBe(false);
  expect([ran, heard]).toEqual([["snapshot.run"], 2]);
  expect(snapshotPanel({ base: "https://b.example/", fetch: send }).querySelector("button")).toBe(null);
  // A fetch that fails is said, not left as a blank panel.
  const down = snapshotPanel({ base: "https://b.example/", fetch: async () => { throw new Error("offline"); } });
  await down.ready;
  expect(down.textContent).toBe("The snapshot files could not be read: offline");
  const none = snapshotPanel({ base: "https://b.example/", fetch: async () => new Response("", { status: 404 }) });
  await none.ready;
  expect(none.textContent).toBe("No snapshot yet.");
  expect(snapshotPanel({}).textContent).toBe("Open this on a Brain to see its snapshots.");
  return "2 sources shown";
}
